Appendix B
Standardized Academic Writing Rubric (SAWR)
The Standardized Academic Writing Rubric (SAWR) was used to evaluate learners’ writing performance before and after the intervention.
Criterion	Score 1 (Beginning)	Score 3 (Developing)	Score 5 (Proficient)
Task Achievement	Response is incomplete or does not address the task effectively.	Main ideas are presented but some aspects remain underdeveloped.	Fully addresses the task with relevant and well-developed ideas.
Organization	Ideas lack clear structure and logical progression.	Basic organization exists but transitions may be limited.	Ideas are logically structured with effective progression.
Coherence & Cohesion	Limited connection between ideas; weak use of linking devices.	Uses basic cohesive devices with occasional repetition.	Smooth connections between ideas with effective transitions.
Vocabulary Use	Limited vocabulary with frequent inappropriate choices.	Adequate vocabulary with some variety.	Precise, varied, and contextually appropriate vocabulary.
Grammar & Academic Style	Frequent grammatical errors affect clarity.	Some grammatical issues remain but meaning is generally clear.	Accurate grammar with appropriate academic style.
Total score range: 5–25 points
